  "jobTitle": "Chief Scientist and Software Engineer",
  "summary": "Over half of my life has been devoted to becoming formally educated in classroom milieus. I spent the normal thirteen years as a student in kindergarten through twelfth grade, eight years as an undergraduate student, and ten years as a graduate student. I have undergraduate and some graduate education in three different fields of human endeavor, namely, chemistry, computer science, and software engineering. I consider myself fairly well versed in several other areas of knowledge including among others: biology, history, mathematics, political science, physics, psychology, religion, and sociology. I have been fascinated by the physical sciences, in particular, chemistry and physics, since my childhood and teenage years, respectively. I fell in love with computer science and computer programming much later in my life. I have over thirty years of experience in computer programming primarily using the functional, object-oriented, and procedural computer language paradigms. The functional languages I have used are Common LISP and Scheme. The object-oriented languages that I prefer are C++, C#, and Java. The procedural languages include BASIC, C, FORTRAN, Modula-2, and Pascal.\n\nMy last job entailed me branching out into the wonderful world of information technology, specifically personal computer maintenance, computer networks, computer network administration, and computer network security. I instructed several information technology technical college classes and essentially took the courses along with the students.",
